{"id":"s1","level":5,"levelName":"Structure and style","n":1,"of":6,"title":"Joining clauses","titleHe":"מִשְׁפָּט מְחֻבָּר","goal":"Use שֶׁ, כִּי and כְּדֵי to build sentences longer than one clause.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"שֶׁ is the workhorse. Glued to the front of a clause it does the job of English that, which and who all at once — and unlike English, it is never optional."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"אֲנִי חוֹשֵׁב שֶׁהוּא צוֹדֵק.","en":"I think (that) he's right."},{"he":"הָאִישׁ שֶׁבָּא אֶתְמוֹל","en":"the man who came yesterday"},{"he":"הַסֵּפֶר שֶׁקָּרָאתִי","en":"the book (that) I read"},{"he":"כְּשֶׁהִגַּעְתִּי, הוּא כְּבָר הָלַךְ.","en":"When I arrived, he'd already left."}]},{"type":"table","caption":"Connectors","head":["Hebrew","English"],"rows":[["שֶׁ","that, which, who"],["כִּי","because"],["כְּדֵי","in order to"],["אֲבָל","but"],["לִפְנֵי שֶׁ","before"],["אַחֲרֵי שֶׁ","after"],["בִּגְלַל שֶׁ","because of the fact that"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"אֲשֶׁר is שֶׁ in literary dress — same meaning, separate word, and everywhere in older prose. When you meet it, read it as שֶׁ."}],"vocab":[{"he":"שֶׁ","en":"that, which, who","translit":"she-"},{"he":"כִּי","en":"because","translit":"ki"},{"he":"אֲשֶׁר","en":"that, which (literary)","translit":"asher"},{"he":"כְּדֵי","en":"in order to","translit":"kdei"},{"he":"אֲבָל","en":"but","translit":"aval"},{"he":"לָכֵן","en":"therefore","translit":"lachen"},{"he":"לְמָשָׁל","en":"for example","translit":"lemashal"},{"he":"בְּעֶצֶם","en":"actually","translit":"be'etsem"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["please, you're welcome","soul, self","that, which, who","city"],"correct":2,"prompt":"שֶׁ","translit":"she-"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["thus","ready, prepared","because","good morning"],"correct":2,"prompt":"כִּי","translit":"ki"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["of","that, which (literary)","in order to","woman"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אֲשֶׁר","translit":"asher"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["in order to","must, need to","thus, so","four (m.)"],"correct":0,"prompt":"כְּדֵי","translit":"kdei"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["teaches","but","one (m.)","and she said"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אֲבָל","translit":"aval"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["specifically, of all things","birthday","therefore","small"],"correct":2,"prompt":"לָכֵן","translit":"lachen"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["(marks a definite object)","four (m.)","for example","with"],"correct":2,"prompt":"לְמָשָׁל","translit":"lemashal"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “because”?","options":["כִּי","כֶּלֶב","לוֹ","פֶּן"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["כִּי","because"],["אֲשֶׁר","that, which (literary)"],["שֶׁ","that, which, who"],["לָכֵן","therefore"],["לְמָשָׁל","for example"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “that, which (literary)”?","options":["יֶלֶד","אֵם","שָׁעָה","אֲשֶׁר"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"כִּי","translit":"ki","en":"because"},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["לָכֵן","בְּעֶצֶם","כִּי","לְמָשָׁל"],"correct":2,"say":"כִּי","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “for example”?","options":["שׁוֹמֵעַ","יֶלֶד","לְמָשָׁל","דֶּלֶת"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “in order to”?","options":["כְּדֵי","נוֹסֵעַ","לוֹ","שָׁלוֹם"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"build","tokens":["כְּבָר","כְּשֶׁהִגַּעְתִּי,","הָלַךְ","הוּא"],"answer":["כְּשֶׁהִגַּעְתִּי,","הוּא","כְּבָר","הָלַךְ"],"en":"When I arrived, he'd already left."},{"type":"build","tokens":["הָאִישׁ","אֶתְמוֹל","שֶׁבָּא"],"answer":["הָאִישׁ","שֶׁבָּא","אֶתְמוֹל"],"en":"the man who came yesterday"}]}